# ── Rust native core ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cargo build output. This is the only large artifact in `core/` — it reaches
# several GB, so without this line a `git add -A` tries to stage the lot.


# cargokit's build_tool is a Dart *package*, not an app, so its lockfile is
# not committed. Its `.dart_tool/` dirs are already covered by the global
# `.dart_tool/` rule above, as is `._target` by the `._*` rule.
rust_builder/pubspec.lock

# Deliberately NOT ignored, despite being generated — CI runs neither
# `cargo` nor `flutter_rust_bridge_codegen`, so a fresh clone can only build
# if these are in the repo:
#   core/src/frb_generated.rs   (declared by `mod frb_generated;` in lib.rs)
#   lib/src/rust/**             (imported directly by Dart)
# Commit core/Cargo.lock too: this is an application, so the exact dependency
# graph should be reproducible.
# Rust core build output
core/target/
rust_builder/**/.cargokit*
.agents/

**/.thumbs/     